    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0494" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.D1/215</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative on the Committee for
                        Refugees From Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Chamberlain</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-28"
                            >February 28, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Phillips</hi>: I have just read your
                    letter of February 21, answering my inquiry regarding the possibility of a
                    contribution by the Government of the United States to the expenses of the High
                    Commission for Refugees Coming from Germany.</p>
                <p>I had a talk with Mr. McDonald while he was here on his way to South America. He
                    tells me that since so few of the other countries have agreed to make a
                    contribution, that he thinks it would be wiser not to attempt at this session to
                    take the action which I suggested.</p>
                <p>If the more important Governments are ready to make a contribution to the
                    expenses of the High Commission, I assume that there will be a different
                    situation presented.</p>
                <p>Appreciating your frankness, I am,</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. P. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chamberlain</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
